 "card": "Prevents bitcoind from abruptly crashing via std::terminate when block or undo writes fail due to disk storage errors such as a full disk. BlockManager now explicitly flushes buffered writers within try-catch blocks to route errors to standard shutdown procedures, and BufferedWriter clears pending buffer offsets before writing to avoid re-triggering writes during stack unwinding. The author observed repeated crashes on 1 TB benchmark servers running out of space and provided a reproducer demonstrating that write failures now exit cleanly.",
